// r0_write.hex
//
// HAZARD UNDER TEST
//   Writes to r0 are discarded, and every path that could leak a write back
//   onto a read of r0 stays shut. There are three such paths and this program
//   exercises all three:
//
//     1. The write port itself. register_file guards on write_addr != 0, so
//        the storage never changes. The r0_is_zero invariant also checks this
//        on every cycle of every program.
//
//     2. The forwarding unit, at distance 1. Index 1 reads r0 in the cycle the
//        discarded write sits in EX/MEM. forwarding_unit guards on
//        ex_mem_rd != 5'd0; without that guard ForwardRs would go to 01 and
//        hand 0x1234 to the ALU.
//
//     3. The write-first bypass, at distance 3. Index 3 reads r0 in the same
//        cycle the discarded write is in WB. This is the interesting one: the
//        bypass condition reg_write && write_addr == rs_addr is genuinely TRUE
//        here, because both addresses are 0. Only the fact that the r0 test
//        comes first in the conditional chain keeps the read at zero. Put the
//        bypass ahead of the r0 test and this test fails while every other
//        test still passes.
//
// EVIDENCE
//   r9 and r10 carry the verdict, and they are independent: r9 fails if the
//   forwarding guard is missing, r10 fails if the write-first bypass is ordered
//   ahead of the r0 check. Each would read 0x1234 ORed into its immediate.
//   Nothing after index 3 writes either register.
//
// POSITIVE CONTROL
//   r9 = 0x55 and r10 = 0x66 are themselves the controls: a value of 0 in
//   either would mean the instruction never ran, and the expected values are
//   distinct from both 0 and the poisoned 0x1234 pattern, so a pass cannot be
//   confused with a program that did nothing.
//
// INDEPENDENT WITNESS
//   dmem word 0. Reset leaves it 0x00000014, and index 7 stores r0 there, so
//   0x00000000 proves both that the store executed and that r0 read as zero
//   through the store-data path.
//
// EXPECTED FINAL STATE
//   r0        = 0x00000000     never written, also asserted every cycle
//   r9        = 0x00000055     <-- 0x00001255 if the forwarding r0 guard fails
//   r10       = 0x00000066     <-- 0x00001266 if write-first precedes the r0 test
//   dmem[0:3] = 0x00000000
//   stalls    = 0              no lw, so the interlock must never fire
//
// 0: ori r0, r0, 0x1234     attempted write to r0, must be discarded
34001234
// 1: ori r9, r0, 0x0055     distance-1 read of r0: tests the forwarding guard
34090055
// 2: nop
00000000
// 3: ori r10, r0, 0x0066    distance-3 read of r0: tests write-first ordering
340A0066
// 4: nop
00000000
// 5: nop
00000000
// 6: nop
00000000
// 7: sw  r0, 0(r0)          witness: word 0 must go from 0x14 to 0
AC000000
// 8: nop
00000000
// 9: nop
00000000
